          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b0248d3f47c813d236f98cc9659f7a422a5c8f9df6b6e58f385b82acf0967880:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e6835cd86696483e995256342bf9713f",
      "statement": "There is no compatibility path for older files: JSON member names are matched exactly without case folding, so a file written by an older build that spelled members Edits/Enabled matches nothing and reads as an empty list, which the code treats as the intended start-over shape.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://SigilLoadout/editservice.go#L211-L222",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d34627cb2aa18d2a8f8fa76675f1091e34dc2b4f10fffdd80e26e1d13f556772:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_dd5fe624a32f431aa9c7c8b017425008",
      "statement": "Unknown JSON members in the edit list are ignored rather than rejected, which is the json/v2 default and is deliberate rather than an oversight.",
